From 10d025115492a7ddfbf64b75da6da9690e4dc612 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicolas Le Bayon <nicolas.le.bayon@st.com>
Date: Tue, 5 Mar 2024 18:24:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 051/572] feat(st-rif): add STM32MP2x support in RIFSC driver

Adapt RIFSC driver to support all STM32MP2 variants, with specific
RIFSC IDs- in semaphore list, and maximum ID.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/arm-trusted-firmware.git 2b2c2d55301d0a5fe776436a80c24864f4feb2f7 feat(st-rif): add STM32MP2x support in RIFSC driver]
Signed-off-by: Nicolas Le Bayon <nicolas.le.bayon@st.com>
Change-Id: Ice244c4518c0b657d625bd7269ea6ad9a04e80c6
---
 drivers/st/rif/stm32_rifsc.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/st/rif/stm32_rifsc.c b/drivers/st/rif/stm32_rifsc.c
index a77429ba76..7b79171a5f 100644
--- a/drivers/st/rif/stm32_rifsc.c
+++ b/drivers/st/rif/stm32_rifsc.c
@@ -19,7 +19,15 @@ void stm32_rifsc_ip_configure(int rimu_id, int rifsc_id, uint32_t param)
 {
 	uint32_t bit;
 
+#if STM32MP21
+	assert(rifsc_id < STM32MP21_RIFSC_MAX_ID);
+#endif /* STM32MP21 */
+#if STM32MP23
+	assert(rifsc_id < STM32MP23_RIFSC_MAX_ID);
+#endif /* STM32MP23 */
+#if STM32MP25
 	assert(rifsc_id < STM32MP25_RIFSC_MAX_ID);
+#endif /* STM32MP25 */
 
 	bit = BIT(rifsc_id % U(32));
 
-- 
2.53.0

